    "Functional capacity of <4 METs is linked to increased risk for perioperative cardiac events regardless of disability type (e.g., CAD, HF). Stress tests may be needed in these cases, especially before surgery if high-risk myocardial ischemia is suspected or as part of pre-surgery evaluation. However, routine preoperative stress testing is not recommended for patients at low risk for cardiac issues due to cost and lack of improved outcomes. Exercise stress testing is preferred if possible due to fewer reversible defects but can still indicate risk levels. Fixed defects do not impact postoperative cardiac events but do signify CAD presence.": [],
